# Presentation-golden corpus manifest for Spyro 2 (fields as in
# games/spyro-1/corpus/presentation-corpus.manifest: name|start|interval|freeze|pins).
#
# attract-demo has no bk2: the row is the plain boot, the title screen and the
# attract demo, which need no input. A movie-less row takes its length from its
# last pin, so every frame it wants is pinned.
#
# The pins are the demo's level-loaded stretches, read off the native terrain
# feed's per-present triangle count over a 19583-VBL boot. The count holds at
# 1985 between segments (the title-screen world) and departs from it while a
# demo level is resident: 3304-3722, 3726-4358, 6450-7774, 9866-11684,
# 13776-15316 and 17408-18558. Each pin sits inside one of those stretches,
# clear of its load transient, so the row covers five distinct levels of world
# geometry and texture data. The grid samples between them hold the
# title-screen world.
# 4358 is a camera cut: the demo's second segment ends with the camera stepping
# 98094 world units in one tick, with every drawn record carrying a previous
# tick of its own. The intermediate leg there shows the previous tick for the
# whole interval; the canonical leg is unaffected.
# 1273 and 1973 are the title screen: the logo sprite and the "press start"
# text, linked into the ordering table at an explicit depth slot
# (func_8001B354) rather than at the head (func_8001B390); pinned for the
# slotted-insert hook. Pins below start are unioned with the grid.
# 1057 is the boot scene before the title: under --lod extended the distant
# low-poly spires between the left cliffs and the skull do not draw, where
# --lod original and the guest reference draw them (64533 px differ).
attract-demo|3973|3000||1057,1273,1973,3973,4358,7073,10773,14573,17973
# attract-demo@heldfade: a present of the held-fade loop after the entry at
# 3232 (isbg=0, one subtractive quad per VBL over the held picture).
attract-demo@heldfade|3234|100|freeze|3236
# attract-demo@sparx-bubble: Aquaria Towers underwater, Sparx inside its air
# bubble; the bubble's front lies between Sparx and the camera (the guest
# reference shows Sparx through the bubble).
attract-demo@sparx-bubble|3880|1000||3880,3881,3920,4040
# attract-demo@meshwarp: the attract demo warped from Metropolis, which draws
# a tracer mesh, to Mystic Marsh at VBL 14600. A stale mesh vertex-list
# address equals the live moby 8019728c (class 0x27B, an animated banner); a
# second capture under that key in one tick would hold the moby at its tick
# pose on sub-tick presents.
attract-demo@meshwarp|15440|1000||15440,15460,15500,15560|OPENPETE_LEVELWARP_TEST=14600:mystic_marsh PRESENTATION_LEG_TIMEOUT=900
# attract-demo@tracerdepth: on sub-tick presents the Metropolis tracer mesh
# was depth-tested at the tick's depth while the camera closed in, drawing it
# in front of terrain (about 221 px at VBL 14581, alpha 0.5).
attract-demo@tracerdepth|14580|2||14581
# attract-demo@tracernear: two Metropolis tracer ribbon segments enter from
# the bottom edge with one end behind the near plane; the cut end's position
# sets the width taper along the whole visible segment (about 700 px at 14299
# and 14301).
attract-demo@tracernear|14299|2||14299,14301
#
# autumn-plains-skelos-badlands-portal-entry: a portal entry from the home
# world, the in-gameplay level change. 1723 is the portal transition, 1823 and
# 1923 the flight with the treasure tally, 2123 the flight with the level name,
# 2273 the arrival cutscene in the entered level.
# 1646, 1658, 1712 and 1774 are the transition's quiet regime edges: the ticks
# where g_GameState steps -1 -> 0 -> 1 -> 2 and 6 -> 7, each stepping the
# camera by at most 116 world units, three orders under the cut guard's
# position threshold and inside its rotation threshold. The pair across such an
# edge spans two simulation regimes rather than one motion, so the
# intermediate leg holds the previous tick instead of lerping the chord; the
# canonical leg is unaffected.
autumn-plains-skelos-badlands-portal-entry|1723|200||1423,1424,1425,1646,1658,1712,1723,1774,1823,1923,2123,2273
# @tcache / @tcsqueeze: the retained terrain cache forced on (llvmpipe refuses it
# otherwise) across a level edge; @tcsqueeze also sizes every arena primary at
# 32768 elements (OPENPETE_TC_INITIAL_CAP) so the arenas grow mid-level. Coverage
# rows of the arena-growth path: the image must match the unsqueezed run.
autumn-plains-skelos-badlands-portal-entry@tcache|1723|200||1723,2273|OPENPETE_TERRAIN_CACHE_FORCE=1 OPENPETE_TC_BAKE_BUDGET_US=off
# @tcbudget0: the first-touch bake budget at 0 (one sector baked per tick), pinned
# through bake-in, where deferred sectors are drawn by the CPU walk beside
# retained ones; a change at that seam moves these tiles. The other
# cache-forced rows turn the budget off, since a wall-time budget makes the
# walked set differ between runs.
autumn-plains-skelos-badlands-portal-entry@tcbudget0|1361|200||1361,1375,2265|OPENPETE_TERRAIN_CACHE_FORCE=1 OPENPETE_TC_BAKE_BUDGET_US=0
autumn-plains-skelos-badlands-portal-entry@tcsqueeze|1723|200||1723,2273|OPENPETE_TERRAIN_CACHE_FORCE=1 OPENPETE_TC_INITIAL_CAP=32768 OPENPETE_TC_BAKE_BUDGET_US=off
# @vram: the two presents of the destination load (VBLs 1349 and 1350) whose
# scene holds no triangle of the game's, no retained terrain, no retained
# backdrop and no held clear, so the compose shows the PSX VRAM framebuffer
# (compose.vram in the tile census). The presents around them compose: 1347,
# 1348 and 1351 to 1356 an empty scene over a kept backdrop or held clear,
# 1357 on the destination's world.
autumn-plains-skelos-badlands-portal-entry@vram|1349|1000||1349,1350
#
# colossus-ice-skating: the player on the Colossus rink with the mirrored copy
# under the ice. 1494, 1694 and 1734 are intermediate legs whose tick pair spans a
# body keyframe advance; 1696 is the leg after one.
colossus-ice-skating|1473|200||1494,1503,1694,1696,1734
# colossus-ice-skating@wall: the player beside the rink's wall, VBL 1886;
# native draws the mirrored copy's tail and horns but not its body under
# the player, which the guest draws. Blessed pre-fix.
colossus-ice-skating@wall|1886|200||1886

# summer-forest-collect-orb: the orb pickup with the 3D orb HUD icon at the
# bottom edge. 1455 is the reported tick where the guest frames the orb icon
# with four golden facets and the native draws the orb alone; 1443 and 1467
# bracket it. The bk2 is 1457 frames, so the grid stops at 1459.
summer-forest-collect-orb|1455|2||1443,1455,1467
#
# shady-oasis-flame: two flame breaths in Shady Oasis. The flame's primitives
# are written at VBL 1415-1431 (peak 1419) and 1533-1549 (peak 1537); 1421 is an
# intermediate leg inside the first breath.
shady-oasis-flame|1413|200||1419,1421,1423,1537
#
# flame-charge: a flame breath in Autumn Plains followed at once by a charge,
# with the breath's smoke puffs on screen through the charge. Over VBL
# 1433-1479 the particle routine stamps class-0 records whose ordering key
# (SZ3 >> 5) - size - 2 is not positive and then appends no primitive for
# them (partsdraw.s:745, :753), up to 8 per tick. 1449 and 1450 are ticks with
# such records; 1430 and 1466 bracket the stretch, 1434 opens it.
flame-charge|1425|25||1430,1434,1449,1450,1466
#
# open-pause-menu: the pause menu open over Summer Forest, 1473 and 1491. The
# menu box is an opaque flat quad under ten tiled panels, a frame and six
# rows of sprite text; the guidebook page beside it carries quad-form glyphs
# (the level banner, the two gem-row slashes).
open-pause-menu|1473|200||1473,1491
#
# open-guidebook: the guidebook open on its contents page, 1553 and 1571. The
# right-hand column (entry names, placeholder dashes, per-cent signs) is
# quad-form glyph text; the digits are sprite text. 1500 and 1503 are inside
# the pause panel's page turn (1494-1504, func_8004BF94 folding every primitive
# of the panel after it is emitted): the panel's glyph text folds with the page.
open-guidebook|1533|200||1500,1503,1553,1571
#
# glimmer-pogo-dialogue: the first dialogue in Glimmer. At 1573 the large
# semi-transparent text box and the speaker's name box are both open; the
# large box's four corners are the stepped corner pieces. 1273 is the title
# fly-in before the level, where the game's logo slides in at the top.
# 1470, 1474 and 1476 straddle Pogo's blend from anim 0 into anim 3 (the id
# changes at 1476); 1560 and 1562 straddle two NPCs' blend from anim 0 into
# anim 1: the intermediate legs show whether the sub-tick pose is continuous
# across a tick while the game blends toward the next animation.
glimmer-pogo-dialogue|1473|200||1273,1470,1474,1476,1560,1562,1573
# Pause menu mid-level: the framebuffer window copies draw buffer 0 at VBL
# 2042 and shrinks over 2027-2042 from full screen to the lower-left
# quarter; pins at the first full-window frame, mid-shrink and settled.
# Synthesized: idle to 2023 then Start (make_bk2.py --hold 2023:2033:Start).
pause-menu-midlevel|2013|200||2027,2035,2073
# pause-menu-midlevel@shrink: the same movie pinned on every VBL of the shrink and the
# settle (one game tick per VBL): the window must show the scaled image of
# the tick being drawn, not the first shrink tick's scene. Blessed pre-fix.
pause-menu-midlevel@shrink|2013|200||2027,2028,2029,2030,2031,2032,2033,2034,2035,2036,2037,2038,2039,2040,2041,2042,2043,2044,2045,2046,2047,2048,2049
# pause-menu-midlevel@shrink-freeze: the first shrink steps with the frozen-world
# backdrop, so the 16:9 side strips show whether the window's border stays inside
# the 4:3 window (without the backdrop the strips are black and hide it).
pause-menu-midlevel@shrink-freeze|2013|200|freeze|2027,2028,2029
# pause-unpause: Start again at 2173; the game grows the window back over
# 2190-2197 from the other draw buffer, then draws the live world. Blessed
# pre-fix. 2192 is the first grow step after the draw buffer's image is
# stored: its cells were fed in texel space at 2191 and in image pixels at
# 2192, and the intermediate leg shows whether they pair across that change
# (the window between the 9/16 and 10/16 boxes) or stand at 10/16.
pause-unpause|2173|200||2189,2191,2192,2193,2195,2197,2199
# colour-cheat-red: the pause-menu colour cheat (Up Right Down Left Up Square
# R1 R2 L1 L2 Up Left Down Right Up, then Circle) sets D_800698CC to 1, and
# from VBL 2328 on the tick writer stores 0xA0000090 at g_Spyro+0x20: the player
# draw cues the model colour table toward far colour (0x90, 0, 0) at IR0 0xA00.
colour-cheat-red|2400|100||2400,2401,2500,2600
# big-head-cheat: the pause-menu big head cheat (Up x4, R1 x4, Circle) sets
# D_800698BE; the player draw scales the head matrix by D_800698C0 (2.0)
# (spyrodraw.s 0x800422A4), which the native player part transform omits.
big-head-cheat|2400|100||2300,2400
# flat-cheat: the pause-menu flat cheat (Left Right Left Right L2 R2 L2 R2
# Square) sets D_800698BF; the player draw scales the body matrix's first
# column by 0x200 (spyrodraw.s 0x800421C8), which the native path omits.
flat-cheat|2400|100||2300,2400
# credits-cheat: the pause-menu credits cheat from Summer Forest (Square,
# Circle x3, then Left, Right x3) reaches the credits at VBL 2264. 3678 and
# 4572 are sub-tick presents with credits letters flying in and departing:
# the draw compacts the CreditsLetter records in states 1-3 into consecutive
# moby slots, so a departing or reused record moves every later letter to
# another slot.
credits-cheat|2300|200||3678,4572
#
# start-new-game: same-moby self-interpenetration. Two faces of one
# moby that cross in 3D show their crossing contour under true depth, where
# the PSX paints each face whole in OT order; the same-moby rank applies the
# game's paint order between such faces only. At 665 a pink sliver shows
# through a near dark shape. Start 1043 (the movie is 1046 VBLs) keeps the grid
# to two samples.
start-new-game|1043|10||665
# start-new-game@fade: the fade from the opening cutscene to the storybook
# picture and its hold. 1013 and 1014 follow the repeat present at 1012: the
# game draws an empty cleared table into the buffer off screen while the
# display keeps the storybook drawn at 1011, so both show the picture of 1012.
# The guest reference rasters the cleared table and is black there.
start-new-game@fade|982|1000||982,988,1012,1013,1014,1016
# start-new-game-cutscene-skip@hold: the same storybook hold after the skipped
# cutscene, at its second picture: the repeat present at 1214 is followed by
# 1215 and 1216, which keep the picture of 1214 (1217 is the fade's next
# step).
start-new-game-cutscene-skip@hold|1214|1000||1214,1215,1216,1217
# intro cutscene, VBL 1667: one of the sheep's eyes is covered by its own
# face geometry (native); the guest draws the eye.
intro-sheep-eye|1657|10||1667|--skip-to-cutscene intro
# intro cutscene, VBL 2170-2178 at 16:9: on intermediate presents the static
# tree moby on the left leaves the screen and returns.
intro-tree-subtick|2170|2||2170,2172,2173,2174,2175,2176,2178|--skip-to-cutscene intro
# intro_arrival cutscene, VBL 1703-1719: a face of the left green wall gem
# flickers as the camera moves, the gem and the wall it is set into trading
# visibility at the gem's outline (native); the guest's outline is steady.
intro-arrival-gem|1701|2||1709,1710,1711,1712,1713|--skip-to-cutscene intro_arrival
# intro_arrival cutscene, VBL 1983-1989: the base of the portal moby slides
# against the ground terrain from tick to tick (native).
intro-arrival-portal-base|1979|2||1983,1984,1985,1986,1987,1988,1989|--skip-to-cutscene intro_arrival
# intro cutscene at 32:9, VBL 1595-1599: two terrain faces at the far right
# of the frame do not draw (native).
intro-32x9-farright|1591|2||1595,1597,1599|--skip-to-cutscene intro --aspect 32:9
# intro_arrival cutscene, VBL 5829-5833: the roof of Ripto's mouth speckles
# dark through its red face (native); the guest draws it clean.
intro-arrival-ripto-mouth|5823|2||5829,5831,5833|--skip-to-cutscene intro_arrival
# crush_intro cutscene, VBL 1585: orb geometry stretches across the screen
# on the sub-tick view (native); the canonical tick draws clean.
crush-intro-orb-stretch|1577|2||1583,1584,1585,1586,1587|--skip-to-cutscene crush_intro
# crush_intro cutscene, VBL 2176: on a camera cut the mobys vanish for a
# moment on the sub-tick view (native); the canonical ticks draw them.
crush-intro-cut-mobys|2170|2||2174,2175,2176,2177,2178|--skip-to-cutscene crush_intro
# summer_forest cutscene, VBL 1912-1922: Moneybags (class 5, moby 800e7d80)
# falls toward the dome on track segments of 0x800 world units or more, which
# the sampler places in one tick after a tick at rest; the sub-tick view holds
# each such step as a jump (native), so at 1914, 1918 and 1922 the
# intermediate leg shows the previous tick whole while the banners lerp. 1912
# is the last sixteenth-step interval before the first placed segment.
summer-forest-moneybags-fall|1910|2||1912,1914,1916,1918,1920,1922|--skip-to-cutscene summer_forest
# sunny_beach_intro cutscene, VBL 2776-2786: two mobys draw the chest on
# coincident faces; native shows the plain box (class 10) until 2786 and the
# studded chest (class 17) from 2788, the guest the chest throughout.
sunny-beach-intro-chest-tie|2772|2||2776,2780,2784,2786,2787,2788|--skip-to-cutscene sunny_beach_intro
# attract-demo-spawn-jump: a class 0x1e3 moby placed without a marker the
# native path reads (named residual); the sub-tick view lerps across it.
#
attract-demo-spawn-jump|14612|2||14614,14615,14616,14617,14618
# glimmer-32x9-leftedge: the reported free-camera pose at 32:9; the terrain
# occlusion cull's frustum half bounded each sector's sphere with a square
# box too small off-axis and culled sector 69 at the left edge (pink
# background). Blessed on the headless-occlusion build, before the fix.
glimmer-32x9-leftedge|2471|2||2473|--skip-to-level glimmer --aspect 32:9 OPENPETE_FREECAM_POSE=30338,87973,7965,-194,52
# glimmer-gem-lamps: Glimmer with both gem-lamp puzzles completed by the
# debug-flags mod's Glimmer row at the first Glimmer tick (the lamps lit with
# their glow, each big gem emitting its orbiting and emitted mobys); the
# movie's Cross presses close the gem cutter's dialogue the completion opens.
# A freecam path (engaged at VBL 2500, one pose per tick) closes on the lamp
# at (31427, 78080) from +X and from 225 degrees at 1000 units a tick, then
# passes the big gem at (32236, 103178). The pins are sub-tick presents where
# the tick depth (OPENPETE_SUBTICK_TICK_DEPTH) moves pixels: 2503 the lamp's
# glow, 2571 and 2579 the gem's tracers.
glimmer-gem-lamps|2500|80||2503,2571,2579|PRESENTATION_MOD=debug-flags:test.apply_tick=1,test.apply_only=Glimmer OPENPETE_FREECAM_AT_VBL=2500 --freecam-path @games/spyro-2/corpus/paths/glimmer-gem-lamps.path
#
# s2-create-save: a new game on a blank card in slot 1 (provisioned formatted
# by the binary in the leg's directory) creates and writes its save. 1022
# ("Accessing MEMORY CARDS") and 1104 ("Creating save block") are presents
# where the game draws nothing: the display shows the last image drawn into
# the buffer it shows, the world under the card box.
s2-create-save|1022|82||1022,1104|--card1 {legdir}/card1.mcr --no-card2
#
# s2-load-save@idol-talisman: Idol Springs portal talisman (class 0x0D9) within view depth 0x800 resolved its flat semi faces to averaging, not additive (card: scripts/make_s2_progress_card.py).
s2-load-save@idol-talisman|2100|2||2100|PRESENTATION_CARD1=games/spyro-2/cards/idol-springs-talisman.mcr --player-pose 120133,78440,37124 OPENPETE_FREECAM_POSE=121646,76475,37070,1452,60 OPENPETE_FREECAM_AT_VBL=2000
#
# idol-springs-level-entry: the level entry from Summer Forest into Idol
# Springs, ending on the loading screen's treasure tally (VBL ~2960-3460; the
# gems fly 2980-3160). The movie ends at 2596 and the row samples the game
# running on without input. In builder state 2 (D_800698F0) the loading
# overlay rebuilds the moby array every tick: one class-1 moby per active
# tally record (*D_80067110, stride 8, active byte +4), then the counter gem
# (+0x0C 0x154, +0x14 0xC00), then the total gem (+0x0C 0xB4). 3060 and 3120
# are sub-tick presents with gems in flight: a spawn or a landing moves every
# later gem to another slot.
idol-springs-level-entry|3000|200||3060,3120
#
# summer-forest-polygon-explosion: Glimmer, Summer Forest, Idol Springs and
# back to Summer Forest through the portals. The movie ends at 4859 and the
# row samples the game running on without input beside the castle. Idol
# Springs places sectors at addresses Summer Forest's decode-cache entries
# hold; a lookup by address alone decoded Idol Springs' vertex words into a
# Summer Forest entry with that entry's counts, and on the return sector 76
# (0x800AF9AC) drew those banks as triangles stretched across the view at
# 5800 and 8000.
# 1935: Glimmer, before the first level change; the sub-tick present draws
# tracer ribbon triangles over the wall at the lower left (1461 px, the whole
# tracer path at that present) at a depth that passes the wall's.
summer-forest-polygon-explosion|5800|2200||1935,5800,8000|PRESENTATION_LEG_TIMEOUT=900

# idol-springs-puzzle-1: Idol Springs with two Zoe zap records live and near
# floor triangles under Spyro (openpete_frame 2000 = VBL 2573; fast boot ends
# at VBL 573). Pins 2195 and 2800 are further ticks with more than one zap
# record live.
idol-springs-puzzle-1|2573|200||2195,2800
# Cutscene letterbox bars growing 2 PSX rows per tick (VBL 1413-1435): the
# intermediate leg must show them between the two ticks. Blessed pre-fix.
riptos_arena-letterbox|1413|2||1415,1425|--skip-to-level riptos_arena
# @res1, @res2vp: the letterbox bars drawn into a --resolution 1 and 2 base
# (512x216 and 1024x432 at 4:3, widened at 16:9), resampled to the capture;
# @res2vp with integer vertex precision, whose implicit pixelation is inert
# under N.
riptos_arena-letterbox@res1|1413|2||1415,1425|--skip-to-level riptos_arena --resolution 1
riptos_arena-letterbox@res2vp|1413|2||1415,1425|--skip-to-level riptos_arena --resolution 2 --vertex-precision integer
# settings-menu: the settings menu (OPENPETE_MENU_DEMO opens it at boot)
# drawn into the capture by --screenshot-overlays, over summer_forest. Its text is
# the credits font's glyph models, read from WAD.WAD on the disc
# (text_moby.c, GAME_FONT_WAD_MODEL).
settings-menu|2073|100||2073|--skip-to-level summer_forest OPENPETE_MENU_DEMO=1 --screenshot-overlays
# crushs-dungeon (games/spyro-2/bk2/crushs-dungeon.bk2): the floor's far lip
# loses the terrain key contest to the lava behind it under --lod extended
# (per-cell keys on pinned far faces); 1506 is the sub-tick present the
# reporter saw. Blessed pre-fix.
crushs-dungeon|1504|2||1504,1506
# crush-intro-dragon-shores-portal: at 16:9 the Dragon Shores picture (baked
# from an eye off the sky's centre) registers against no sky, so the side
# band shows the flat backdrop; 4169 is the present the reporter saw.
#
crush-intro-dragon-shores-portal|4165|2||4169|--skip-to-cutscene crush_intro
# robotica-farms-spark-wrap: barrel-blast sparks (class-1 streaks) with a
# position halfword just below 0x10000 (Z 0xFFEF, -17 as int16). The routine's
# camera-relative difference wraps through the GTE's int16 load; a build that
# reads the halfword unsigned projects the endpoint ~65000 units off and draws
# a full-height vertical line on the canonical and intermediate legs.
#
robotica-farms-spark-wrap|1921|2||1923,1925,1957,1959|--skip-to-level robotica_farms
# robotica-farms-barrier-ring (games/spyro-2/bk2/robotica-farms-barrier-ring.bk2):
# Spyro, placed on a raised ledge at the level's edge, runs into the boundary
# wall and bounces; the fourth contact's ring (class 0x2CC, 144 additive faces
# in three rings) is in view. Each keyframe re-points every face's colour index
# through a 144-entry faceblock patch list, which fades the rings outward.
# 2147 is the ring fully formed, 2153 the inner ring faded, 2161 the outer
# ring mid-fade. A walk that applies fewer than all 144 entries leaves the
# last faces on the base colour index and draws them as a flat pale band.
#
robotica-farms-barrier-ring|2147|2||2147,2153,2161
# idol-springs-block-glow: Foreman Bud's lights-out blocks (class 0x1E5) in
# Idol Springs. The placement lands Spyro on the block at (109568, 50176),
# which steps its keyframe byte (Moby+0x3C) yellow to unlit at VBL 1722 and
# two neighbours unlit to yellow at 1724, each after about 180 unchanged
# ticks; the free camera engages at 1724, after the step, since it freezes
# the player update. The game changes the face colours in one tick, so pins
# 1726-1732 show the current keyframe's colours on both legs.
idol-springs-block-glow|1726|2||1726,1728,1730,1732|--skip-to-level idol_springs --player-pose 109568,50176,19500,3072@1700 OPENPETE_FREECAM_POSE=107520,57000,21500,3072,300 OPENPETE_FREECAM_AT_VBL=1724
# idol-springs-fish-swallow (games/spyro-2/bk2/idol-springs-fish-swallow.bk2):
# Spyro flames a fish into the idol's mouth after the block puzzle. The
# thrown fish (class 0x19F) takes m_DepthOffset -6 and states 5 then 6 (the
# record is selected 3356-3418); the closing lips are terrain at its depth,
# keyed into its buckets or nearer, so the ordering table paints them over
# the parts of the fish in front of them. 3402 the fish whole in the mouth,
# 3406 and 3408 cut by the lower lip, 3412 and 3418 gone behind the closed
# jaw. The intermediate leg's sub-tick presents 3407, 3411 and 3417 fall
# inside the covered stretch. Blessed pre-fix.
idol-springs-fish-swallow|3402|2||3402,3406,3408,3412,3418
# crushs-dungeon-idle-colour: Crush's Dungeon idle at spawn. The torch-lit
# wall sectors carry keyframe colour descriptors (registry pairs at +0x18 LP
# and +0x28 HP) whose blend factor steps every tick; the glow around the
# torches in the top band changes on every tick. The canonical legs at 3048,
# 3050 and 3052 show the packed colours; the intermediate legs at 3049 and
# 3051 show whether the sub-tick present blends the two ticks' colours or
# holds one tick's. Blessed pre-fix.
crushs-dungeon-idle-colour|3048|2||3048,3050,3052|--skip-to-level crushs_dungeon

# scorch-far-dune-admit: a far dune's low-detail faces (sector 132, faces 0
# and 2) are missing against the sky left of centre, where the PSX draws
# them; the camera is a gameplay camera behind the player near the level's
# checkerboard plaza. Blessed pre-fix.
scorch-far-dune-admit|2471|2||2473|--skip-to-level scorch --aspect 4:3 OPENPETE_FREECAM_POSE=96403,61401,11991,2746,159

# game-over: the last life lost in Breeze Harbor and the game-over screen. The
# game-over picture is four sprites linked behind the player's ordering-table
# slot, so the player draws over it and the text over him. 2400 is the death
# with the life counter, 3000 and 3600 the game-over screen with the player
# on the ledge.
game-over|2400|10000||2400,3000,3600

# Level-entry rows: the level reached by --skip-to-level with no input, one pin
# where the level is resident and running (G_LEVELID = the level, G_GAMESTATE
# -1).
# ocean-speedway-skip-entry: the flight through the ring course, the hoop
# counter and timer HUD, rings and towers over the sea.
ocean-speedway-skip-entry|1773|2||1773|--skip-to-level ocean_speedway
# aquaria-towers-skip-entry: the level start above water (the attract demo
# shows the underwater stretch), Spyro, Sparx and the seahorse mobys.
aquaria-towers-skip-entry|1773|2||1773|--skip-to-level aquaria_towers
# crystal-glacier-skip-entry: the snow field at the start, falling snowflake
# particles, a frozen-in-ice moby.
crystal-glacier-skip-entry|1773|2||1773|--skip-to-level crystal_glacier
# cloud-temples-skip-entry: the start courtyard with the temple walls and the
# NPC mobys.
cloud-temples-skip-entry|1773|2||1773|--skip-to-level cloud_temples
# dragon-shores-skip-entry: the entrance plaza with the gate NPC.
dragon-shores-skip-entry|1773|2||1773|--skip-to-level dragon_shores
# gulps-overlook-fight: the Gulp fight running with no input: Gulp in the
# arena, the boss health bar at the bottom left.
gulps-overlook-fight|2073|2||2073|--skip-to-level gulps_overlook

# @tcforce: rows with no @tcforce twin in freecam-corpus.manifest, with the
# retained terrain cache forced on (OPENPETE_TERRAIN_CACHE_FORCE=1; on the
# software rasteriser terrain otherwise draws through the CPU walk) and the
# first-touch bake budget off, as the @tcforce rows there. A row named after a
# row above is that row's twin.
robotica-farms-spark-wrap@tcforce|1959|2||1959|--skip-to-level robotica_farms OPENPETE_TERRAIN_CACHE_FORCE=1 OPENPETE_TC_BAKE_BUDGET_US=off
scorch-far-dune-admit@tcforce|2471|2||2473|--skip-to-level scorch --aspect 4:3 OPENPETE_FREECAM_POSE=96403,61401,11991,2746,159 OPENPETE_TERRAIN_CACHE_FORCE=1 OPENPETE_TC_BAKE_BUDGET_US=off

# glimmer-skip-scene-split: two game renders reach the native scene in one
# VBL at the boot logo (VBL 0, key 573) and on the --skip-to-level route
# (VBL 730, key 1304: the Demo Mode book).
glimmer-skip-scene-split|573|2||573,1304|--skip-to-level glimmer
